@@ -13,6 +14,21 @@ JSON envelope. A bot may post only to rooms where it has membership. Codes are
 shown in the owner/admin bot list and are not included in other user-facing
 views.
 
-Successful requests respond with `201 Created` and a message resource `Location`.
-Empty request bodies return `422`, invalid room IDs return `404`, and invalid
-or inactive bot codes return `401`.
+A bot can optionally configure a webhook URL. When a person mentions that
+bot in a newly created message, Campfire enqueues an HTTP `POST` to the URL; the
+posting request never waits for the webhook. The JSON payload has `event:
+"mention"`, `author` (`id`, `name`), `room` (`id`, `name`, `reply_to`), and
+`message` (`id`, `body.text`, `body.html`, `link`) fields. `body.text` excludes
+the addressed bot's mention, `body.html` contains the rich-text body, and
+`reply_to` is the bot's own room-scoped message endpoint. Paths are relative to
+the Campfire origin.
+
+A `200` response with `Content-Type: text/plain` or `text/html` posts the
+response body back into the room as the bot. Plain text is treated as text, not
+markup. A `204` response does not post a message; other status codes and media
+types are ignored. Webhook delivery uses a background job and short connection
+and read timeouts, and refuses destinations that resolve to private networks.
+
+Successful direct bot-message requests respond with `201 Created` and a message
+resource `Location`. Empty request bodies return `422`, invalid room IDs return
+`404`, and invalid or inactive bot codes return `401`.
